ntdll: WINEDLLPATH_FIRST, a directory searched before the runtime's modules.

WINEDLLPATH is searched after the runtime's own dll directory, so it cannot
replace a builtin. Riftway's runtime ships DXMT's d3d11, dxgi and d3d10core as
the builtins and Wine's own (wined3d) in lib/wine/wined3d; a game profile that
needs wined3d points WINEDLLPATH_FIRST there. CrossOver has the same need
(CW Hack 24067, prepend_dll_path) but its caller is not in the published sources.

Riftway, offered under LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -388,14 +388,18 @@
 
 static void set_dll_path(void)
 {
-    char *p, *path = getenv( "WINEDLLPATH" );
+    char *p, *path = getenv( "WINEDLLPATH" ), *first = getenv( "WINEDLLPATH_FIRST" );
     int i, count = 0;
 
     if (path) for (p = path, count = 1; *p; p++) if (*p == ':') count++;
 
-    dll_paths = malloc( (count + 2) * sizeof(*dll_paths) );
+    dll_paths = malloc( (count + 3) * sizeof(*dll_paths) );
     count = 0;
 
+    /* Riftway: WINEDLLPATH_FIRST is one directory searched before the runtime's own
+     * modules (WINEDLLPATH comes after them), such as Wine's wined3d-based d3d11, dxgi
+     * and d3d10core for a game DXMT does not run, in a runtime whose defaults are DXMT's. */
+    if (first && *first) dll_paths[count++] = strdup( first );
     if (!build_dir) dll_paths[count++] = dll_dir;
 
